css='body{margin:0;background:#f5f0e8;color:#28232c;font:18px/1.65 Georgia,serif}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:38px 28px}h1{font-size:48px;line-height:1.1}p{max-width:80ch}a{color:#705079}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figure{margin:28px 0}figcaption,small{font-size:15px}figcaption{padding:10px 0}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.pair figure{margin:0}details{border:1px solid #cdc5bd;padding:16px;margin:18px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:bold}.diffwrap{overflow:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:10px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc}.diff{font:12px/1.45 monospace}.diff td{padding:4px}.diff_header{background:#e3ddd4}.diff_add{background:#d3e8d5}.diff_sub{background:#f1d3d2}.diff_chg{background:#f3e6ae}@media(max-width:700px){h1{font-size:34px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Tiling — one mark, different lives</title><style>'''+css+'''</style><main><p>Ada Research · 24 September 2026</p><h1>One mark, different lives</h1><p>A small source becomes a floor, a surrounding pattern and a fabric. This pass keeps that thread and repairs the places where the reading lost its route. The photographs come from inside the museum.</p><nav><a href="#reading">Exact text differences</a><a href="/compose/sources?map=Pattern_Disco&amp;doc=final">Read from the first hall</a><a href="/book-tasks/review?seq=tiling">Review comments</a><a href="DECISIONS.md">Decisions and evidence</a></nav><figure><img src="symmetry-p1-pg.png" alt="The held and live pattern panels with their console inside the patterned museum hall"><figcaption>Held P1 on the left; live PG on the right. The source stays fixed while the reflection and two-row shift change its return.</figcaption></figure><h2>A route through the Foundry</h2><p>The studio now appears where the chapter first asks you to enter it. The longer loom experiments follow under “On a return visit.” Their comparisons remain available, without delaying the first encounter with a pattern that surrounds you.</p><h2>The colour stays; the edge nearly goes</h2><div class="pair"><figure><img src="contrast-neighbours.png" alt="Two grey squares on dark and light backgrounds, with the museum console and nearby coloured forms"><figcaption>Equal target values, unequal surrounds.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="contrast-equal.png" alt="The same museum view with target faces blending into equal grey surrounds"><figcaption>Equal surrounds. Faint raised edges remain.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The review called this disappearance. The photographs make a more precise sentence possible: the faces almost disappear, while the little bodies remain. The surrounding animated work continues in both images.</p><h2>Other works can carry the argument</h2><p>The symmetry chapter now invites comparison with the existing looms, mills, patterned architecture and atlas plates. The makers’ names matter alongside the operations. The wall gallery has seventeen rules available; this loaded hall uses ten group IDs. Its finite selection is not a proof of the full classification.</p><h2>From the wall to a skirt</h2><figure><img src="fabric-studio.png" alt="The source editor, patterned wall and preview dress inside the final Tiling hall"><figcaption>The recipe reaches the skirt while the crown and sleeves keep their own materials. This is the studio’s preview dress.</figcaption></figure><p>The mirror controls now have their actual names in the text, including the return to the walking costume. The ending leads to Change’s curve and two spatial readings. The exit turret keeps its ball-hunting behaviour and this placement excludes the visitor.</p><p>All twelve review items have a recorded decision. Eight chapters now have titles. Four new museum photographs are included in final.md. No artifacts were removed.</p><details><summary>Checks and limits</summary><p><a href="symmetry/report.json">11 symmetry checks</a> · <a href="contrast/report.json">7 contrast checks</a> · <a href="turret/report.json">13 turret checks</a>. The final runs passed and exited normally. The turret uses a supplied XR target contract in a desktop runtime; no tracked-headset interaction or damage test is claimed. Existing renderer and registry warnings remain in the logs. <a href="verification.json">Publication verification</a> · <a href="figure-provenance.json">Exact image provenance</a>.</p><p>The first turret test expected a tracked player that this desktop harness does not create. That result is retained in <a href="turret-desktop-first/report.json">the first report</a>. The corrected test supplies the production resolver’s expected group and node. The earlier distant contrast photographs are also retained.</p></details><h2 id="reading">Exact changes in final.md</h2>'''+''.join(parts)+'''<h2>Comment by comment</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Review item</th><th>Decision</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</tbody></table></main></html>'''
